:''Not to be confused with [[Brainwashed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Titan Cat]].''
'''Malevolent Jamiera Cat''' is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemy that appears in [[Titanic Rampage (Merciless)|The Malevolent Titan]]. It was added in [[Version 12.7 Update|Version 12.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Malevolent Jamiera Cat
|image = E 668.png
|first appearance = [[Titanic Rampage (Merciless)|The Malevolent Titan]]
|money drop = 1,350¢ - 5,332¢
}}

==Enemy==
This short-ranged enemy is fairly slow, boasts a lot of health and frequently deals extreme damage with an Omni Strike that hits all the way up to 320, with a 20% chance to land a Savage Blow that's guaranteed to nuke or gravely cripple everything it catches. It comes with a moderately durable [[Shield]] that fully regenerates each time it is knocked back while blocking status effects, so when it gets to push, it and any support can be difficult to stop. Its [[Counter-Surge]] likewise poses a threat, but ultimately isn't as relevant as its stats and other abilities are enough to fully invalidate most strategies with [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]].

==Strategy==
Because of the sheer damage it outputs, [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] will not stall it too well alone, as neither can even come close to surviving a Savage Blow. It's better to use cheap, disposable meatshields like [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Kyubey Cat (Rare Cat)|Kyubey Cat]] or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]]. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]], [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Macho Cat]] and [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] are especially good options, as they'll be able to stall Malevolent Jamiera in spite of its Savage Blows. [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] is the only non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]] that outranges Malevolent Jamiera, so he is likely the best choice.

As most [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] Uber Rare Cats outrange Malevolent Jamiera, almost any of them will be great choices against it, although [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yaminora]] in particular isn't the best choice due to only barely outranging its Omni Strike. Ubers that can crowd-control him and nullify his heavy pushing power, such as [[Hevijak the Wicked (Uber Rare Cat)|Hevijak]] and [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Summoner Satoru]] will be especially effective.

